#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2527
msgid "This site’s converters handle the building blocks—kilometres vs miles, litres vs other volumes, km/h vs mph for trip pace. Use them to sanitize inputs, then apply a proper economy formula or a dedicated economy calculator when comparing L/100 km to mpg."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2354
msgid "Those printed times are local. Zones and date changes hide the true duration. Use the airline’s block time or convert both instants to UTC before subtracting."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:268
msgid "Three scales, two kinds of zero"
msgstr "三種刻度，兩種零"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1786
msgid "Tide atlases and racing handicaps assume nautical miles and knots. Converting a race course to statute miles without converting the rating math breaks comparisons between seasons and fleets."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2027
msgid "Tile and plank sold in boxes list coverage area per box. Divide required area (with waste) by coverage per box in the same unit, then round up whole boxes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1319
msgid "Tile, plank, and carpet orders usually add 5–15% waste for cuts and mistakes. Apply the waste percentage after you trust the measured area. Converting units does not replace waste planning."
msgstr "瓷磚、木板和地毯訂單通常會因切割和錯誤而增加 5-15% 的浪費。在您信任測量的面積後應用廢棄物百分比。轉換單位並不能取代廢棄物規劃。"

